{"id":"word:hebrew:H6918","type":"word","title":"קָדוֹשׁ","subtitle":"H6918 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"sacred (ceremonially or morally); (as noun) God (by eminence), an angel , a saint , a sanctuary","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to קָדוֹשׁ (H6918) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: a.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 119 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"קָדוֹשׁ (qâdôwsh) means sacred (ceremonially or morally); (as noun) God (by eminence), an angel , a saint , a sanctuary First listed occurrence: 1Sam 2 2."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"קָדוֹשׁ","transliteration":"qâdôwsh","pronunciation":"kaw-doshe'","strong":"H6918","lemmaId":"hebrew:H6918","partOfSpeech":"a","forms":["קְד֥וֹשׁ","קָד֖וֹשׁ","קְד֣וֹשׁ","קָדוֹשׁ֙","קָד֔וֹשׁ"],"morphs":[["HAamsa",46],["HAamsc",27],["HAampa",17],["HTd/Aamsa",4],["HR/Aamsc",4],["HC/Aamsa",3],["HC/R/Aamsc",3],["HAampc/Sp3ms",2],["HC/Aamsc",2],["HR/Aampa",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"sacred (ceremonially or morally); (as noun) God (by eminence), an angel , a saint , a sanctuary","usage":"holy (One), saint.","full":"H6918. qadosh קָדוֺשׁ adjective sacred, holy ; — absolute ׳ק Exod 19:6 +; קָדשׁ 29:31 +; construct קְדוֺשׁ Isa 1:4 +; קְדשׁ 49:7 2 t.; suffix קְדשִׁי Hab 1:12 ; קְדוֺשׁוֺ Isa 10:17 ; 49:7 קְדוֺשְׁכֶם 43:15 ; plural קְדוֺשִׁים Hosea 12:1-2 t., קְדשׁים Lev 11:44 16 t.; suffix קְדשָׁיו Deut 33:3 ; Psa 34:10 , קְדשָׁו֯ Job 15:15 ; &#8212; 1 of God, as separate, apart, and so sacred, holy: a. exalted on theophanic throne Isa 6:3 (3 t. in verse), Psa 22:4 heavenly throne Isa 57:15 ; in victory 5:16 ; 1Sam 2:2 ; Psa 99:3 (|| נוֺרָא ), 99:5 ; 99:9 ; שְׁמוֺ ׳ק וְנוֺרָא 111:9 . b. separate from human infirmity, impurity, and sin: Josh 24:19 (E), 1Sam 6:20 ; Hab 1:12 ; ׳כ אני קדושׁ Lev 11:44-45 , 19:2 ; 20:26 ; 21:8 (H); בְּקִרְבְּךָ קדושׁ Hosea 11:9 ; ׳ק בישׂראל Ezek 39:7 . c. יִשְׂרָאֵל קְדוֺשׁ = divine name (originating from trisagion , Isa 6:3 ) 1:4 ; 5:19 , 24 ; 10:20 ; 12:6 ; 17:7 ; 29:19 ; 30:11-12 , 15 ; 31:1 ; Is :2; 41:14 , 16 , 20 ; 43:3 , 14 ; 45:11 ; 47:4 ; 48:17 ; 49:7 ; 54:5 ; 55:5 ; 60:9 , 14 elsewhere only 2Kin 19:22 = Isa 37:23 ; Jer 50:29 ; 51:5 ; Psa 71:22 ; 78:41 ; 89:19 ; ׳ק יעקב Isa 29:23 , קְדוֺשׁוֺ 10:17 ; 49:7 , קְדוֺשְׁכֶם 43:15 ; קָדוֺשׁ 40:25 ; Hab 3:3 ; Job 6:10 , plural intensive שׁים ( ו ) קד Hosea 12:1 ; Prov 9:10 ; 30:3 . 2. a. of place, sacred, holy , chambers of priests Ezek 42:13 , camp of Israel Deut 23:15 , + מָרוֺם of heaven Isa 57:15 (but of ׳י Du Ry, and [reading ׳בְּק as holy , ב essent.] Klo Che Marti); in following (often defective) pointing dubious, read probably קֹדֶשׁ 2: ק ם ׳ ( ו ) מק of the court of tabernacle, Exod 29:31 ; Lev 6:9 ; 6:19 ; 6:20 ; 7:6 ; 10:13 ; 16:24 ; 24:9 (P), of Jerusalem Eccl 8:10 ; עליון ׳ק מִשְׁכְּנֵי Psa 46:5 ; ׳ק הֵיכָלָ֑ךָ 65:5 . b. persons: priests Lev 21:7-8 , Num 16:5 , 7 (P), Aaron Psa 106:16 , Levites 2Chr 35:3 , prophet 2Kin 4:9 , Nazirite Num 6:5 , 8 (P), Israel ק ׳גּוֺי Exod 19:6 (E), ק ׳עם Deut 7:6 ; 14:2 , 21 ; 26:19 ; 28:9 ; כָּלהָֿעֵדָה Num 16:3 (P); remnant in Jerusalem Isa 4:3 ; קדשׁים sacred Lev 11:44-45 , 19:2 ; 20:7 , 26 ; 21:6 ; Num 15:40 ; קדשׁים sacred ones, saints Deut 33:3 (song), Psa 16:3 ; 34:10 ; Dan 8:24 . c. angels , Psa 89:6 ; 89:8 ; Job 5:1 ; 15:15 ; Zech 14:5 ; Dan 8:13 (twice in verse). d. קדשׁים מים Num 5:17 holy water . e. time ( ׳לי ) ק ׳הַיּוֺם Neh 8:9-10 , 11 ; י ׳קְדוֺשׁ Isa 58:13 , of Sabbath. &#8212; (compare Biblical Aramaic קַדִּישׁ ). קדשׁ (√ of following; ᵑ7 Syriac; see Biblical Hebrew id. , קָדוֺשׁ ).","rootNote":"or קָדֹשׁ ; from 6942 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Sam 2 2","keyReferences":["1Sam 2 2","1Sam 6 20","2Chr 35 3","2Kgs 4 9","2Kgs 19 22","Dan 8 13","Dan 8 13","Dan 8 24"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":119,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Sam 2 2","b